🌐WEBSITE INFO
We encourage you to upload your poster to the Poster Harvester, but it is not mandatory. The abstracts and posters will be live on the website by the last week of August. If ou choose to upload your poster, you must have it uploaded by September 28, 2026. 

For publishing purposes, the poster upload to the Poster Harvester must be a PDF file at the highest resolution possible. The complete poster is limited to one side only. This means one single page for your PDF file. Fonts should be sans-serif (e.g. Arial, Calibri, etc.). Minimum font size should not be smaller than 6pt. 

Please label your poster file upload in this manner: Poster Number_Presenter’s Last Name (example: M-002_Redmond). If you do not label your poster this way, it may not get uploaded correctly to our new ACoP abstract repository after the conference.
You may record poster audio in the Poster Harvester for the ACoP website. Attendees will hear the audio when they view the poster and it creates a more personal and engaging experience. There is a task you will see the task for Poster Audio. You will have a maximum of 3 minutes that you can record. Again, this is optional. 

